From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:59:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: BetterVR 1.0.0 builds into PS5-ECAM's Cemu as a host
 module

CEMU_PS5 takes the platform, the OpenXR runtime over hmd2 and the stand-ins from the port
(port/bettervr/module.cmake) in place of platform_linux.cpp and the vendored OpenXR loader, whose
headers stay; no libatomic link (the port defines the generic atomic functions).

- the one graphics queue's lock (ps5xr::QueueMutex) around the mod's own submit
- libc++ 18: no ranges::contains, no floating-point from_chars (strtod), no gettid
- the log also goes to the app's boot log; Cemu's settings are not shared with a second file
- no update check
